      "thunderSemantics": "fxptn2 dispatch; EBP holds pre-update target counter; stored counter zero initializes rand%5, then advances unless rand%3 is zero; draw bolt (old/2)%5 and impact old%4; old>=20 ends. Bolt bottom aligns tile bottom. Caster counter0..9, modulo5,40px at tile-4.",
      "areaSemantics": "SetArea positive mask uses Area+1-abs(dx)-abs(dy); CheckMagicTarget uses request center for positive cast distance and enumerates X outer/Y inner. Positive weights select only explicitly permitted targets; weights do not define damage. Client adapter bounds candidates at255 and map edges.",
      "casterAndTargetSemantics": "Magic() sets caster +1DC/+1E0 once before checking BYTE target count, including zero targets; the target loop writes each target +174/+1C4, replacing its previous effect. Latest caster spell replaces the previous charge; unrelated target effects remain. Pattern6 has the same fxptn2 strips as pattern5; their native source caster charge is shared, not restarted for every target.",
      "unit8Semantics": "CheckMagicTarget Unit8 resolves clicked unit, truncates ID/10*10, enumerates slots0..8 in ID order, writes XY=-1,-1, succeeds even with zero valid slots. Adapter retains explicit permission and known live unit guards; native +0/+4 flags and full relationships are not reconstructed by inferred HP alone. Caller positive cast mask applies to selected cell, not every group member.",
      "tornadoSemantics": "fxptn3: each target old counter0..9 draws impact old%4, then increments. Coordinate registration precedes target update, keyed by effect type/clickXY; post counter1..9 draws3 vortices,10 none, final target clear resets to0 and that coordinate pass draws0 once. Next pass has no target registration. Native modulo15 insertion cursor is also inclusive render-prefix bound, preserving wrap behavior. Coordinate function fixes lookup801, uses count4 frames, radius rand%50+20, angle rand%360, signed trunc(r*cos/sin+.5), bottom-aligned64px. Original global RNG/wall-clock are not recreated."
    },
